Mutation order audit on S130 row bank
  rows=749; true key is M-1/14=e/(14q)
  product-value is literal (p*q)/q=p, not the old p*q payload.
  product_value       agree= 88234 flip= 71462 tie=120430 score=21207/40018
  sum_value           agree=258329 flip=     0 tie=21797 score=538455/560252
  denominator_power   agree=170095 flip= 88234 tie=21797 score=361987/560252
  numerator_power     agree=148543 flip=109786 tie=21797 score=318883/560252
  readout: sum-value is theorem-safe because it is 1+M; product-value is not
  order-safe but it is a branch scheduler after e=1; power mutations are
  magnitude stress tests and should not be proof denominators.

