Tournament Analysis
  vertices: the four literal Farey mutations
  pairwise observable: retained proof role vector
    (order safety, branch scheduling, packet side-channel, magnitude stress, false-quotient detection)
  switch/gauge: larger role vector wins; ties use listed Hamiltonian order
  fingerprint: score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1} directed_3cycles=0
  Hamiltonian path: sum_value > product_value > numerator_power > denominator_power
  challenged assumption: the numerator-times-denominator mutation is useless
    as a value, but after the e=1 quotient it is exactly the numerator p,
    which is the C27/K33 route switch.

Proof-route readout
  1. Keep exact M=p/q and e=14p-q first.
  2. If e=0, route to AP/GW boundary equality.
  3. If e=1, the literal product mutation collapses to p and schedules:
       p=1 -> q-parent/right-neighbor, p=2 -> C27 petal/two-block,
       p>=3 -> K33/state-lift/Fejer packet.
  4. Use sum-value only as an affine check that a quotient preserved M.
  5. Use the two power mutations as adversarial stress tests: a claimed
     tournament or scalar invariant surviving those distortions is probably
     too magnitude-blind and needs endpoint/Ramanujan/Fejer labels restored.
  This integrates HYP-2931/HYP-2940 with HYP-2981/HYP-2982/HYP-2983:
  Farey mutations are front-end schedulers; Fejer/Ramanujan/Kaczynski
  packets are the certificate back end.
